.TH XD\-MSCONFIG 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-msconfig \- System Configuration Utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-msconfig
.OP \-\-page N
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-msconfig
is Windows XP's System Configuration Utility (\fBmsconfig\fR, which the
Run dialog also finds it as), for what starts when you log on.
It is listed in Administrative Tools.
.TP
.B General
Normal Startup turns every startup program and user service on;
Selective Startup shows what the other tabs leave on (Load User Services,
Load Startup Items), and clearing either box turns that whole list off.
XP's Diagnostic Startup and its SYSTEM.INI, WIN.INI and BOOT.INI settings
have nothing to stand for in a desktop session and aren't there.
.TP
.B Services
The systemd user services enabled into
.IR default.target ,
.I graphical\-session.target
or
.IR xeondesktop\-session.target ,
through the user manager's D\-Bus interface, and those turned off here
before.
Clearing one disables it; ticking it enables it again.
Services enabled for every user (in
.IR /etc/systemd/user )
are greyed: only an administrator can turn them off.
.TP
.B Startup
XDG autostart entries that apply to this desktop (OnlyShowIn and NotShowIn
against
.BR $XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP ,
TryExec, X\-systemd\-skip), the system's and your own, with their command
and folder.
Clearing a system entry writes your own copy of it with
.B Hidden=true
(the autostart specification's way); ticking it removes that copy again.
.B Add...
adds an installed program or a command line as your own entry;
.B Remove
deletes one of your own entries.
.PP
As in Windows, changes count from the next log on; OK offers to log off.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-page " N"
Show the Nth tab, from 0 (General, Services, Startup).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/autostart/*.desktop
Your startup programs, and your copies hiding the system's.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_DIRS/autostart/*.desktop
The system's (usually
.IR /etc/xdg/autostart ).
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xeondesktop/startup.ini
The user services turned off here, which stay listed so they can be
turned on again.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd\-xdg\-autostart\-generator (8),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR xd\-services (1),
.BR xd\-admintools (1)
